'''''Calle Mura''''' ({{Literal translation|Wall Street}}) is a street in the [[Ampurias]] borough of [[Castejón]]. It runs parallel to the [[Tistaina Canal]] for its entire length. Urban decay following the [[1982 Tava Morotí earthquake]] led to it being fully pedestrianized in the late 1980s, and now forms part of the [[Tistaina Riverwalk]].

The street takes it's name from the [[W:Palisades|palisades]] which existed on the street from 1553 to the 1800s, first constructed during the ''[[Guardafui]]'' period when [[La Frontera|''La Frontera'']] remained relatively unexplored by Mesogean colonists. The walls were gradually dismantled as the city expanded. By the late 19th century, both residences and businesses occupied the area, but increasingly the latter predominated as residential growth shifted to [[Expansión]]. During the 20th century, several [[W:Early skyscrapers|early skyscrapers]] were built on Calle Mura, including [[Empuria World Building]], once the world's tallest building. The street is near multiple [[Castejón Metropolitan Rapid Transit|metro]] stations, [[W:Water taxi|water taxi]] stops, and [[W:Passenger terminal (maritime)|ferry terminals]].

